      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 800</span><span class="rf-text">Settlers from the Marquesas and greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a> have reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaiian Islands</a> by this date, bringing their religious beliefs</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1200</span><span class="rf-text">By tradition Pāʻao, a priest or chief from Tahiti, arrives in Hawaiʻi and brings the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapu-hawaiian-culture">kapu</a> system</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1819</span><span class="rf-text">After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-i">Kamehameha the Great</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ka-ahumanu">Kaʻahumanu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keopuolani">Keōpūolani</a> confer with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahuna">kahuna</a> nui <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hewahewa">Hewahewa</a> and persuade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-ii">Liholiho</a>, Kamehameha II, to overthrow the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapu-hawaiian-culture">kapu</a> system</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1820</span><span class="rf-text">Protestant Christian missionaries begin to arrive from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and gain great influence in the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1930s</span><span class="rf-text">The American author Max Freedom Long originates the philosophy and practice he calls <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huna-people">Huna</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1976</span><span class="rf-text">Members of Protect Kahoʻolawe ʻOhana file suit over the Navy's use of Kahoʻolawe for target practice, citing cultural and religious sites</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1988</span><span class="rf-